OL,3,AUK falls silent to mark Armistice Day
OL,4,
OL,5,FThe UK has fallen silent to mark
OL,6,FArmistice Day, commemorating the end of
OL,7,FWorld War One.
OL,9,FThe two-minute silence took place to
OL,10,Fmark the end of the war and to remember
OL,11,Fthose who have died in conflicts.
OL,13,FDefence Secretary Wes Streeting laid a
OL,14,Fwreath at the Cenotaph memorial in
OL,15,FLondon, which was also attended by
OL,16,Fsenior military figures, schoolchildren
OL,17,Fand cadets.
OL,19,FIn Staffordshire, the Duke and Duchess
OL,20,Fof Gloucester also laid a wreath during
OL,21,Fthe service at the Royal British Legion
OL,22,FNational Remembrance Gardens.
